# Agent & Frontend Integration Guide: `django-social-autoposter` (v0.1.1)

A standalone Django REST Framework package for broadcasting social media posts at once to Facebook, Instagram, X (Twitter), LinkedIn, and more.

---

## 🔒 Authentication
All endpoints require DRF token authentication:
```http
Authorization: Token <user_token>
# OR
Authorization: Bearer <jwt_access_token>
```

---

## 📡 REST API Endpoints

### 1. Broadcast Post to All / Selected Platforms
* **Endpoint:** `POST /social/broadcast/`
* **Request Payload:**
```json
{
  "title": "Exciting Announcement",
  "message": "We have just released our new platform features! Check it out now.",
  "link_url": "https://example.com/announcement",
  "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/sample.jpg",
  "platforms": ["facebook", "twitter", "linkedin", "instagram"]
}
```
> **Tip:** You can omit the `"platforms"` array or pass `null` to automatically post to all platforms currently enabled in `.env` or the database.

* **Response (HTTP 201 Created):**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Exciting Announcement",
  "message": "We have just released our new platform features! Check it out now.",
  "link_url": "https://example.com/announcement",
  "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/sample.jpg",
  "target_platforms": ["facebook", "twitter", "linkedin", "instagram"],
  "content_type": null,
  "object_id": null,
  "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:30:00Z",
  "logs": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "broadcast": 1,
      "platform": "facebook",
      "status": "published",
      "external_post_id": "109876543210_12345",
      "external_post_url": "https://facebook.com/109876543210_12345",
      "error_message": null,
      "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:30:02Z"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "broadcast": 1,
      "platform": "twitter",
      "status": "published",
      "external_post_id": "1840000000000000000",
      "external_post_url": "https://x.com/i/web/status/1840000000000000000",
      "error_message": null,
      "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:30:02Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

### 2. View Broadcast History
* **Endpoint:** `GET /social/broadcast/`
* Returns all past broadcasts with nested status logs.

### 3. Filter Execution Logs
* **Endpoint:** `GET /social/logs/?platform=facebook&status=failed`
* Filters audit logs by platform (`facebook`, `instagram`, `twitter`, `linkedin`) or status (`published`, `failed`, `pending`, `skipped`).

### 4. Twitter / X OAuth 1.0a User Context Requirements
Twitter's `POST /2/tweets` endpoint requires **OAuth 1.0a User Context** tokens (or OAuth 2.0 User Context). Bearer Tokens (App-Only) are rejected with 403 Forbidden.
Required tokens in `.env` or `SocialPlatformConfig`:
- `TWITTER_API_KEY`: Consumer Key
- `TWITTER_API_SECRET`: Consumer Secret
- `TWITTER_ACCESS_TOKEN`: User Access Token
- `TWITTER_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET`: User Access Token Secret

⚠️ **Developer Portal Permission Warning**: In [developer.x.com](https://developer.x.com/) under Project & App settings -> **User authentication settings**, permissions must be set to **"Read and write"** before generating/regenerating the tokens.
